From f200251eb27f3d0058b518d23d28ded5bb27132f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "suricata.lu" <suricata.lu@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 17:16:08 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] mlinux: Use the new set_monitor_channel prototype from
 6.12.101

Linux 6.13 added a struct net_device argument to
cfg80211_ops.set_monitor_channel (upstream 9c4f830927750a2bf9fd9426a5257f0fdce3b662,
"wifi: cfg80211: pass net_device to .set_monitor_channel"). The driver
selects the new prototype only when CFG80211_VERSION_CODE is 6.13.0 or
later.

The 6.12 stable series backported that change in v6.12.101, as a
dependency of 2b0eab425e1f ("wifi: cfg80211: convert pmsr_free_wk to
wiphy_work to fix deadlock"). CIP kernels from v6.12.101-cip29 on have
the new prototype, and the driver no longer builds:

  moal_sta_cfg80211.c:524:32: error: initialization of
  'int (*)(struct wiphy *, struct net_device *, struct cfg80211_chan_def *)'
  from incompatible pointer type
  'int (*)(struct wiphy *, struct cfg80211_chan_def *)'
  [-Wincompatible-pointer-types]

Select the new prototype from 6.12.101. Kernels 6.12.0 to 6.12.100,
including NXP linux-imx 6.12.49 without CIP, keep the old prototype.
The function does not use the new argument.

Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 mlinux/moal_sta_cfg80211.c | 6 ++++--
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/mlinux/moal_sta_cfg80211.c b/mlinux/moal_sta_cfg80211.c
index 21092c2..dbe0f99 100644
--- a/mlinux/moal_sta_cfg80211.c
+++ b/mlinux/moal_sta_cfg80211.c
@@ -127,7 +127,8 @@ rmp_table_t rmp_table_sta_6G[] = {
 #ifdef UAP_SUPPORT
 #if CFG80211_VERSION_CODE >= KERNEL_VERSION(3, 8, 0)
 static int woal_cfg80211_set_monitor_channel(struct wiphy *wiphy,
-#if CFG80211_VERSION_CODE >= KERNEL_VERSION(6, 13, 0)
+/* 6.12.101 stable backported the 6.13 net_device argument */
+#if CFG80211_VERSION_CODE >= KERNEL_VERSION(6, 12, 101)
 					     struct net_device *dev,
 #endif
 					     struct cfg80211_chan_def *chandef);
@@ -699,7 +700,8 @@ static const struct wiphy_coalesce_support coalesce_support = {
 #ifdef UAP_SUPPORT
 #if CFG80211_VERSION_CODE >= KERNEL_VERSION(3, 8, 0)
 static int woal_cfg80211_set_monitor_channel(struct wiphy *wiphy,
-#if CFG80211_VERSION_CODE >= KERNEL_VERSION(6, 13, 0)
+/* 6.12.101 stable backported the 6.13 net_device argument */
+#if CFG80211_VERSION_CODE >= KERNEL_VERSION(6, 12, 101)
 					     struct net_device *dev,
 #endif
 					     struct cfg80211_chan_def *chandef)
-- 
2.43.0

